This is the N+1 pattern — the #1 item on the runbook's "things that have burned us" list. The old code did one batched query (`order_id__in=order_ids`) then grouped in memory; the new code fires a separate `OrderItem` query per order inside the loop. Step 4: grep the log to confirm the per-order queries started firing at the deploy.
